🚽 collide.brainrot — axis-aligned bounding boxes.
🚽
🚽 Deliberately scalar-only. A `gang Rect *` parameter would be the natural
🚽 shape, but the semantic analyser reverses the parameter list for any
🚽 function with struct-pointer parameters, so a two-rect signature would
🚽 be rejected when called correctly and accepted when called with the
🚽 arguments swapped. Eight chads it is. See DESIGN.md C3.

🚽 Boxes are (x, y, w, h) with y measured downward from the top of the
🚽 screen. Touching edges count as overlapping.
cap aabb(chad ax, chad ay, chad aw, chad ah,
         chad bx, chad by, chad bw, chad bh) {
    edgy (ax + aw < bx) { bussin L; }
    edgy (bx + bw < ax) { bussin L; }
    edgy (ay + ah < by) { bussin L; }
    edgy (by + bh < ay) { bussin L; }
    bussin W;
}
